Package: plurx-player
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${python3:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}, libdovi3 (<< 3.4~), python3 (>= 3.10), zenity
Recommends: desktop-file-utils, mesa-vulkan-drivers | vulkan-icd
Built-Using: ${plurx:Built-Using}
Description: Dolby Vision playback of plurx titles on Linux
 plurx Player plays titles handed over from the plurx web app ("Open titles
 in: plurx Player") in mpv, keeping the original Dolby Vision stream for
 profile 5 and 8 titles and receiving profile 7 FEL titles as profile 8.1.
 .
 Dolby Vision is mapped for the screen with plurx's closed-form CM v4.0 and
 CM v2.9 display management, the same equations the plurx server uses,
 targeting the compositor's reported luminance and the largest standard
 gamut inside the panel's primaries.
 .
 It carries its own build of mpv and libplacebo in /usr/lib/plurx-player.
 The distribution's mpv and libplacebo, and every program linked against
 them, are untouched.
 .
 HDR output needs a Wayland compositor with wp_color_manager_v1 in HDR mode,
 such as GNOME in HDR mode. An accurate target luminance needs a compositor
 that reports the panel's real luminance; stock compositors may report a
 default instead.
